---
description: Keep web, Cursor preview, Vercel, and Capacitor iOS in sync
alwaysApply: true
---

# Platform parity (web + native + preview)

Fit Finder has **one UI** in `web/src/` and **one backend** in `supabase/`. Three runtimes share the same code:

| Runtime | How it runs | `isNativePlatform()` |
| ------- | ----------- | -------------------- |
| Cursor preview / `npm run dev` | Next.js dev server | `false` (web) |
| Vercel | `npm run build` (SSR + API proxy) | `false` (web) |
| iOS | `CAPACITOR_BUILD=true` static export in WKWebView | `true` (native) |

**Cursor preview is web, not iOS.** After UI changes, run `cap:sync` and smoke-test the simulator for native-only paths (deep links, localStorage auth, direct Supabase calls).

## Backend calls — always use shared invokers

| Use case | Module | Never |
| -------- | ------ | ----- |
| Edge Functions (analyze, parse, delete account, …) | `web/src/lib/invoke-function.ts` | Raw `fetch("/api/…")` or direct Supabase URL in components |
| Product API (analyze, parse) | `web/src/lib/api.ts` (wraps invoke-function) | Reimplement scoring in UI |

- **Web / preview / Vercel:** `invokeFunction` → `/api/functions/<name>` (session from cookies).
- **Native iOS:** `invokeFunction` → `${NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL}/functions/v1/<name>` with JWT + apikey headers.

When adding a new privileged backend operation:

1. Add a Supabase Edge Function under `supabase/functions/`.
2. Register it in `supabase/config.toml` (`verify_jwt = true`).
3. Add the name to `ALLOWED` in `web/src/app/api/functions/[name]/route.ts`.
4. Call it via `invokeFunction()` from client code.

## Auth — dual path by design (do not collapse without testing both)

| | Web / preview | Native iOS |
| - | ------------- | ---------- |
| Client | `@supabase/ssr` cookies (`supabase/client.ts`) | `@supabase/supabase-js` + localStorage |
| Magic link PKCE | Server `/api/auth/callback` | Client `/auth/callback` + `fitfinder://` deep link |
| Session refresh | `proxy.ts` middleware | Client auto-refresh |

Auth changes must be tested on **web magic link** and **iOS simulator magic link** separately. Guard native-only code with `isNativePlatform()`; guard web-only PKCE redirect with `!isNativePlatform()`.

## Navigation

| Situation | Use |
| --------- | --- |
| Normal in-app navigation (web) | Next `router.push` / `replace` |
| Cross-route recovery on iOS static export | `navigateApp()` from `navigate-app.ts` |
| Auth deep links on iOS | `router.replace` in `capacitor-bridge.tsx` (not full page load) |

## Environment variables

Use **`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`** only (no `VITE_*`). Same `web/.env.local` values for dev, Vercel, and `cap:sync` (inlined at build time).

## QA parity

- Splash QA: on in dev; Vercel Preview by default; native when `NEXT_PUBLIC_ENABLE_SPLASH_QA=true` at `cap:sync` time.
- First-launch reset: `?firstLaunch=1` on any platform; Splash QA → “Reset first launch (full)” when QA is enabled.

## Checklist after changes

**UI / `web/src/`:** run `cd web && npm run cap:sync` (see `capacitor-ios-sync.mdc`).

**Backend / `supabase/functions/`:** deploy functions; no cap:sync unless UI also changed.

**Verify both builds:**

```bash
cd web && npm run build:verify
```
